  "caption_latex": "Supporting spin readout for the continuous-feedback controls of main Fig.~2. The left column [{(a,c,e)}] uses uniform number losses $(0.2,0.2,0.2)\\omega_c$; the right column [{(b,d,f)}] uses weak-end losses $(0.04,0.52,0.04)\\omega_c$. {(a,b):} Connected endpoint correlations $G_{13}^{xx}$. {(c,d):} Fidelity $F_{\\Phi^+}$ with the fixed Bell state: the shaded region above $1/2$ certifies entanglement using three raw spin-correlation moments. {(e,f):} Concurrence $\\mathcal C_{13}$ of the averaged endpoint state. Curves compare feedback off, continuous feedback and independent drive noise; the weak-end column also includes the matched detection coefficient control. The $J_b=0$ line is shown in {(a,b,e,f)}, where factorisation fixes it to zero; it is omitted from {(c,d)}, where factorisation does not imply zero fidelity. All coloured curves are deterministic total-photon-cap-five references. Like-for-like panels use matched scales.",
